From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Date: Sat, 30 Aug 2026 03:23:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] isvp: move SPI NOR env offset to 0x30000

The boot partition is 192K, so the env partition lives at 0x30000. The
2013.07 tree is built via the LEGACY build system, which ignores
configs/uboot/layout/sfcnor.config entirely -- BR2_TARGET_UBOOT_CONFIG_FRAGMENT_FILES
is forced unset by configs/fragments/uboot/v2013-07.fragment, and Buildroot
only consumes that fragment list under the Kconfig build system. So the
fragment value never reached this bootloader: it still read and wrote its
env at the old 0x40000, which now lies inside the backup partition.

Point the SPI NOR backend at 0x30000 to match the firmware layout.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
 include/configs/isvp_common.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/configs/isvp_common.h b/include/configs/isvp_common.h
index b3b5407f..ff247080 100644
--- a/include/configs/isvp_common.h
+++ b/include/configs/isvp_common.h
@@ -613,7 +613,7 @@
 #define CONFIG_ENV_SIZE			(32 << 10)
 #define CONFIG_ENV_OFFSET		(CONFIG_SYS_MONITOR_LEN + CONFIG_SYS_MMCSD_RAW_MODE_U_BOOT_SECTOR * 512)
 #elif defined(CONFIG_ENV_IS_IN_SPI_FLASH)
-#define CONFIG_ENV_OFFSET		0x40000
+#define CONFIG_ENV_OFFSET		0x30000
 #define CONFIG_ENV_SIZE			0x8000
 #define CONFIG_ENV_SECT_SIZE		0x8000
 #else
